{"type":"match","data":{"path":{"text":"./pages/downloads/edges.tsv"},"lines":{"text":"pathwaymech:MetaCyc_PWY-7722_sulfoed-edge-034_e32ea33b2de3\tUniProtKB:P0DOV5\tpathwaymech:enables\tRHEA:47897\tbiolink:Association\tinfores:pathwaymech\tknowledge_assertion\tmanual_validation_of_automated_agent\tPMID:26195800|PMID:39840830|UniProtKB:P0DOV5\tFunctional protein/activity relation, not monomer sufficiency. The 2025 recombinant SQ1 enzyme is tetrameric in solution and crystals. Minor NADP activity and trace G6P activity are assay-dependent side activities outside the native NAD-dependent step.\t\"[{\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"UniProtKB:P0DOV5\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"ECO:0000269, PMID26195800: this reviewed SQ1 gene product is assigned the specified catalytic activity; its cited genomic and experimental references explicitly name strain SQ1.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"/comments/1/reaction; /references/0/referenceComments; /references/1/referenceComments\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"PMID:26195800\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"SQ1 IMG0090 was cloned and purified from recombinant E. coli; it oxidized SQ to SGL with a strong NAD+ preference. Whole-pathway reconstitution used the purified protein.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"//*[@id=\\\"\"s4\\\"\"]/p[1]; //*[@id=\\\"\"s5\\\"\"]/p[2]; Figure 4B; SI Heterologous Overproduction and Purification of His-Tagged Proteins\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"PMID:39840830\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"The codon-harmonized SQ1 SQDH construct has a tetrameric solution state by SEC-MALLS (~119 kDa versus ~28 kDa monomer), consistent with its crystals. The published untagged sequence equals P0DOV5.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"//*[@id=\\\"\"s2-2\\\"\"]/p[1]; Figure 4; //*[@id=\\\"\"s5-2\\\"\"]; //*[@id=\\\"\"s5-3\\\"\"]/p[1]\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"PMID:39840830\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"Under the 2025 kinetic conditions, NAD+ was favored over NADP+ by about 10^6 in catalytic efficiency, and very weak G6P turnover was detectable at high enzyme concentration; the 2015 negative assay is condition-specific.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"//*[@id=\\\"\"s2-1\\\"\"]/p[1]; //*[@id=\\\"\"s2-1\\\"\"]/p[2]; Table 1\"\"}]\"\t\"[{\"\"id\"\": \"\"PMID:26195800\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"e82307720415251fbe81a8293ed7078effeb5e268502c5776ce9b30f632e8afc\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Original 2015 full primary article including SI methods, tables and figure legends in publisher-deposited PMC HTML; retrieved 2026-10-11\"\", \"\"title\"\": \"\"Entner-Doudoroff pathway for sulfoquinovose degradation in Pseudomonas putida SQ1.\"\", \"\"url\"\": \"\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4534283/?pdf=render\"\"}, {\"\"id\"\": \"\"PMID:39840830\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"d3059313116aeac892709ea5a759bc1900fc4f47e8d021ff965a5a3c557f36b3\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Original 2025 full primary PMC HTML, including complete construct sequences and Methods; retrieved 2026-10-11\"\", \"\"title\"\": \"\"Structure, kinetics, and mechanism of Pseudomonas putida sulfoquinovose dehydrogenase, the first enzyme in the sulfoglycolytic Entner-Doudoroff pathway.\"\", \"\"url\"\": \"\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12133307/?pdf=render\"\"}, {\"\"id\"\": \"\"UniProtKB:P0DOV5\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"c39828a60a1c3ba040a95bd392a9d1514fa8b2134cf5d1bc2fa7ae475b9ebd24\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Complete reviewed entry JSON retrieved 2026-10-11; entry version 25, sequence version 1; last annotation 2026-09-02\"\", \"\"title\"\": \"\"Sulfoquinovose 1-dehydrogenase\"\", \"\"url\"\": \"\"https://rest.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P0DOV5.json\"\"}]\"\n"},"line_number":9070,"absolute_offset":10772889,"submatches":[{"match":{"text":"Entner-Doudoroff"},"start":2292,"end":2308},{"match":{"text":"Entner-Doudoroff"},"start":2846,"end":2862}]}}
{"type":"match","data":{"path":{"text":"./pages/downloads/edges.tsv"},"lines":{"text":"pathwaymech:MetaCyc_PWY-7722_sulfoed-edge-035_84fb7a58a7b5\tUniProtKB:P0DOV6\tpathwaymech:enables\tRHEA:47909\tbiolink:Association\tinfores:pathwaymech\tknowledge_assertion\tmanual_validation_of_automated_agent\tPMID:26195800|UniProtKB:P0DOV6\tFunctional activity assignment. Divalent-metal binding below is a reviewed similarity inference, not an SQ1 metal-titration measurement. No physical monomer or oligomer state is inferred from the native MONOMER frame name.\t\"[{\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"UniProtKB:P0DOV6\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"ECO:0000269, PMID26195800: this reviewed SQ1 gene product is assigned the specified catalytic activity; its cited genomic and experimental references explicitly name strain SQ1.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"/comments/1/reaction; /references/0/referenceComments; /references/1/referenceComments\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"PMID:26195800\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"Purified recombinant SQ1 IMG0091 converted SGL to SG in sequential reconstitution. Minor spontaneous hydrolysis was also observed before lactonase addition; it does not replace the enzyme-supported native step.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"//*[@id=\\\"\"s5\\\"\"]/p[1]; //*[@id=\\\"\"s5\\\"\"]/p[2]; Figure 4B-C\"\"}]\"\t\"[{\"\"id\"\": \"\"PMID:26195800\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"e82307720415251fbe81a8293ed7078effeb5e268502c5776ce9b30f632e8afc\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Original 2015 full primary article including SI methods, tables and figure legends in publisher-deposited PMC HTML; retrieved 2026-10-11\"\", \"\"title\"\": \"\"Entner-Doudoroff pathway for sulfoquinovose degradation in Pseudomonas putida SQ1.\"\", \"\"url\"\": \"\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4534283/?pdf=render\"\"}, {\"\"id\"\": \"\"UniProtKB:P0DOV6\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"c2c78a34870f5edbf56ec4d4ee56fe715cdebad570050ffcb8e159b87a378ab9\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Complete reviewed entry JSON retrieved 2026-10-11; entry version 21, sequence version 1; last annotation 2026-06-10\"\", \"\"title\"\": \"\"6-deoxy-6-sulfogluconolactonase\"\", \"\"url\"\": \"\"https://rest.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P0DOV6.json\"\"}]\"\n"},"line_number":9071,"absolute_offset":10776212,"submatches":[{"match":{"text":"Entner-Doudoroff"},"start":1476,"end":1492}]}}
