//pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4534283/?pdf=render\"\"}, {\"\"id\"\": \"\"UniProtKB:P0DOV7\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"0566981bd12cca55a07e8a7bb627a5798bbb41859b6168e9aaf2a2f6e6e02ee8\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Complete reviewed entry JSON retrieved 2026-10-11; entry version 26, sequence version 1; last annotation 2026-09-02\"\", \"\"title\"\": \"\"6-deoxy-6-sulfo-D-gluconate dehydratase\"\", \"\"url\"\": \"\"https://rest.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P0DOV7.json\"\"}]\"\n"},"line_number":9072,"absolute_offset":10778222,"submatches":[{"match":{"text":"Entner-Doudoroff"},"start":1674,"end":1690}]}}
{"type":"match","data":{"path":{"text":"./pages/downloads/edges.tsv"},"lines":{"text":"pathwaymech:MetaCyc_PWY-7722_sulfoed-edge-037_3022be361192\tUniProtKB:P0DOV8\tpathwaymech:enables\tRHEA:47925\tbiolink:Association\tinfores:pathwaymech\tknowledge_assertion\tmanual_validation_of_automated_agent\tNCBIProtein:KHL76360.1|PMID:26195800|PMID:41830472|UniProtKB:P0DOV8\tFunctional assignment of the reviewed SQ1 gene product. The 2015 cloned IMG00100 gene uses an upstream start relative to the current GenBank annotation at the same locus. Native prose has stale R-SLA/family annotations; current native reaction and Rhea/UniProt chemistry select S-SLA. No monomer sufficiency is asserted.\t\"[{\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"UniProtKB:P0DOV8\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"ECO:0000269, PMID26195800: this reviewed SQ1 gene product is assigned the specified catalytic activity; its cited genomic and experimental references explicitly name strain SQ1.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"/comments/1/reaction; /references/0/referenceComments; /references/1/referenceComments\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"PMID:26195800\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"Purified recombinant SQ1 IMG0100 cleaved KDSG to SLA and pyruvate. Pyruvate was verified by a positive lactate-dehydrogenase assay and HPLC cochromatography; the SLA assay was not enantiomer-resolved.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"//*[@id=\\\"\"s5\\\"\"]/p[1]; //*[@id=\\\"\"s5\\\"\"]/p[2]; Figure 4D-E\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"PMID:26195800\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"The cloned IMG00100 used forward primer CACCATGTCCACTGCTGTCACG. All recombinant inserts came from SQ1 chromosomal DNA and were sequence-verified; the paper does not specify current UniProt accessions.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"//*[@id=\\\"\"si8\\\"\"]/p[1]; Table S2, PpSQ1_00100f row\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"NCBIProtein:KHL76360.1\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"The original SQ1 protein record locates PpSQ1_00455 at complement(JTCJ01000004.1:18793..19560). This is the current annotated gene call, not a claim that its N terminus equals the longer 2015 construct.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"/GBSet/GBSeq/GBSeq_feature-table/GBFeature[GBFeature_key=\\\"\"source\\\"\"]/GBFeature_quals; /GBSet/GBSeq/GBSeq_feature-table/GBFeature[GBFeature_key=\\\"\"CDS\\\"\"]/GBFeature_quals; /GBSet/GBSeq/GBSeq_sequence\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"PMID:41830472\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"The 2026 P. putida aldolase abstract reports a homohexamer, optimal Co/Mn activity and modest KDPG cross-reactivity. The accessible abstract does not expose its strain or construct sequence; these details are contextual and are not transferred as direct SQ1 assembly/metal assignments.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"/resultList/result[0]/abstractText\"\"}]\"\t\"[{\"\"id\"\": \"\"NCBIProtein:KHL76360.1\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"8736f6a5439a022c10f154cafdeb607f32515739d029ccbfe72020b7bf5165e7\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Original accession-version GBSet/GBSeq XML retrieved 2026-10-11; sequence and strain/CDS identity only, automated original functional name not imported\"\", \"\"title\"\": \"\"SQ1 PpSQ1_00455 protein and genomic CDS annotation\"\", \"\"url\"\": \"\"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=protein&id=KHL76360.1&rettype=gb&retmode=xml\"\"}, {\"\"id\"\": \"\"PMID:26195800\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"e82307720415251fbe81a8293ed7078effeb5e268502c5776ce9b30f632e8afc\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Original 2015 full primary article including SI methods, tables and figure legends in publisher-deposited PMC HTML; retrieved 2026-10-11\"\", \"\"title\"\": \"\"Entner-Doudoroff pathway for sulfoquinovose degradation in Pseudomonas putida SQ1.\"\", \"\"url\"\": \"\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4534283/?pdf=render\"\"}, {\"\"id\"\": \"\"PMID:41830472\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"bfaee9c036939b4db87a8076aacfcebd894569f3f7a31fab54d5a28b49a3c055\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Original 2026 primary abstract only, through Europe PMC single-PMID core JSON; full article/SI unavailable and deposited structure API requests returned404; retrieved 2026-10-11\"\", \"\"title\"\": \"\"Metal-Dependent 2-Keto-3,6-dideoxy-6-sulfo-gluconate (KDSG) Aldolase: Decoding the Key C-C Bond Cleaving Step in Bacterial Sulfoglycolysis.\"\", \"\"url\"\": \"\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:41830472%20AND%20SRC:MED&resultType=core&format=json\"\"}, {\"\"id\"\": \"\"UniProtKB:P0DOV8\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"16dc1c10fef8e123b0b42f19cfe81abfbe68e0bd2c534ee6125d425d14e51021\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Complete reviewed entry JSON retrieved 2026-10-11; entry version 21, sequence version 1; last annotation 2026-09-02\"\", \"\"title\"\": \"\"2-dehydro-3,6-dideoxy-6-sulfogluconate aldolase\"\", \"\"url\"\": \"\"https://rest.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P0DOV8.json\"\"}]\"\n"},"line_number":9073,"absolute_offset":10780438,"submatches":[{"match":{"text":"Entner-Doudoroff"},"start":3352,"end":3368}]}}
{"type":"match","data":{"path":{"text":"./pages/downloads/edges.tsv"},"lines":{"text":"pathwaymech:MetaCyc_PWY-7722_sulfoed-edge-038_23672ce28ce9\tUniProtKB:P0DOV9\tpathwaymech:enables\tRHEA:47929\tbiolink:Association\tinfores:pathwaymech\tknowledge_assertion\tmanual_validation_of_automated_agent\tPMID:26195800|PMID:37886098|UniProtKB:P0DOV9\tAlternative NADP- and NAD-dependent final activity, not sequential steps. Current Rhea/UniProt and native reaction sides select S-SLA/S-SL; stale native protein prose links R-SLA. The SQ1 HPLC-MS assay was not an independent enantiomer-resolved characterization.\t\"[{\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"UniProtKB:P0DOV9\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"ECO:0000269, PMID26195800: this reviewed SQ1 gene product is assigned the specified catalytic activity; its cited genomic and experimental references explicitly name strain SQ1.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"/comments/1/reaction; /references/0/referenceComments; /references/1/referenceComments\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"PMID:26195800\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"Purified recombinant SQ1 IMG0088 oxidized SLA to SL with both NAD+ and NADP+. Published kinetic constants used succinate semialdehyde because the SLA concentration was undefined; no SLA Km is assigned here.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"//*[@id=\\\"\"s4\\\"\"]/p[2]; Table 1 and footnote; Figure 4E-F\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"PMID:37886098\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"The later tetramer and stereoselectivity experiments concern Rhizobium leguminosarum SRDI565 RlGabD, not SQ1. They are not transferred as direct assembly or enantiomer-assay evidence for P0DOV9.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"//*[@id=\\\"\"abstract1\\\"\"]/p[1]; //*[@id=\\\"\"sec3\\\"\"]/p[1]; //*[@id=\\\"\"sec6\\\"\"]/p[1]\"\"}]\"\t\"[{\"\"id\"\": \"\"PMID:26195800\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"e82307720415251fbe81a8293ed7078effeb5e268502c5776ce9b30f632e8afc\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Original 2015 full primary article includi