//*[@id=&quot;s2-1&quot;]/p[1]; //*[@id=&quot;s2-1&quot;]/p[2]; Table 1</code></details></li></ul></td></tr><tr id=\"mechanism-edge-35\"><td>6-deoxy-6-sulfogluconolactonase<br><code>UniProtKB:P0DOV6</code></td><td>enables<p>Functional activity assignment. Divalent-metal binding below is a reviewed similarity inference, not an SQ1 metal-titration measurement. No physical monomer or oligomer state is inferred from the native MONOMER frame name.</p></td><td>6-deoxy-6-sulfo-D-glucono-1,5-lactone + H2O =&gt; 6-deoxy-6-sulfo-D-gluconate + H(+)<br><code>RHEA:47909</code></td><td><ul><li><a href=\"#reference-8\">UniProtKB:P0DOV6</a><p><strong>Source assertion:</strong> ECO:0000269, PMID26195800: this reviewed SQ1 gene product is assigned the specified catalytic activity; its cited genomic and experimental references explicitly name strain SQ1.</p><details><summary>Source location</summary><code>/comments/1/reaction; /references/0/referenceComments; /references/1/referenceComments</code></details></li><li><a href=\"#reference-12\">PMID:26195800</a><p><strong>Source assertion:</strong> Purified recombinant SQ1 IMG0091 converted SGL to SG in sequential reconstitution. Minor spontaneous hydrolysis was also observed before lactonase addition; it does not replace the enzyme-supported native step.</p><details><summary>Source location</summary><code>//*[@id=&quot;s5&quot;]/p[1]; //*[@id=&quot;s5&quot;]/p[2]; Figure 4B-C</code></details></li></ul></td></tr><tr id=\"mechanism-edge-36\"><td>6-deoxy-6-sulfo-D-gluconate dehydratase<br><code>UniProtKB:P0DOV7</code></td><td>enables<p>Functional activity assignment; current reviewed homodimer and one [4Fe-4S] cluster annotations are inferred by similarity to Q1JUQ1, not directly measured SQ1 assembly or cluster occupancy.</p></td><td>6-deoxy-6-sulfo-D-gluconate =&gt; 2-dehydro-3,6-dideoxy-6-sulfo-D-gluconate + H2O<br><code>RHEA:47913</code></td><td><ul><li><a href=\"#reference-9\">UniProtKB:P0DOV7</a><p><strong>Source assertion:</strong> E