ents/1/reaction; /references/0/referenceComments; /references/1/referenceComments</code></details></li><li><a href=\"#reference-12\">PMID:26195800</a><p><strong>Source assertion:</strong> Purified recombinant SQ1 IMG0100 cleaved KDSG to SLA and pyruvate. Pyruvate was verified by a positive lactate-dehydrogenase assay and HPLC cochromatography; the SLA assay was not enantiomer-resolved.</p><details><summary>Source location</summary><code>//*[@id=&quot;s5&quot;]/p[1]; //*[@id=&quot;s5&quot;]/p[2]; Figure 4D-E</code></details></li><li><a href=\"#reference-12\">PMID:26195800</a><p><strong>Source assertion:</strong> The cloned IMG00100 used forward primer CACCATGTCCACTGCTGTCACG. All recombinant inserts came from SQ1 chromosomal DNA and were sequence-verified; the paper does not specify current UniProt accessions.</p><details><summary>Source location</summary><code>//*[@id=&quot;si8&quot;]/p[1]; Table S2, PpSQ1_00100f row</code></details></li><li><a href=\"#reference-16\">NCBIProtein:KHL76360.1</a><p><strong>Source assertion:</strong> The original SQ1 protein record locates PpSQ1_00455 at complement(JTCJ01000004.1:18793..19560). This is the current annotated gene call, not a claim that its N terminus equals the longer 2015 construct.</p><details><summary>Source location</summary><code>/GBSet/GBSeq/GBSeq_feature-table/GBFeature[GBFeature_key=&quot;source&quot;]/GBFeature_quals; /GBSet/GBSeq/GBSeq_feature-table/GBFeature[GBFeature_key=&quot;CDS&quot;]/GBFeature_quals; /GBSet/GBSeq/GBSeq_sequence</code></details></li><li><a href=\"#reference-15\">PMID:41830472</a><p><strong>Source assertion:</strong> The 2026 P. putida aldolase abstract reports a homohexamer, optimal Co/Mn activity and modest KDPG cross-reactivity. The accessible abstract does not expose its strain or construct sequence; these details are contextual and are not transferred as direct SQ1 assembly/metal assignments.</p><details><summary>Source location</summary><code>/resultList/result[0]/abstractText</code></details></li></ul></td></tr><tr id=\"mechanism-edge-38\"><td>3-sulfolactaldehyde dehydrogenase<br><code>UniProtKB:P0DOV9</code></td><td>enables<p>Alternative NADP- and NAD-dependent final activity, not sequential steps. Current Rhea/UniProt and native reaction sides select S-SLA/S-SL; stale native protein prose links R-SLA. The SQ1 HPLC-MS assay was not an independent enantiomer-resolved characterization.</p></td><td>(2S)-3-sulfolactaldehyde + NADP(+) + H2O =&gt; (2S)-3-sulfolactate + NADPH + 2 H(+)<br><code>RHEA:47929</code></td><td><ul><li><a href=\"#reference-11\">UniProtKB:P0DOV9</a><p><strong>Source assertion:</strong> ECO:0000269, PMID26195800: this reviewed SQ1 gene product is assigned the specified catalytic activity; its cited genomic and experimental references explicitly name strain SQ1.</p><details><summary>Source location</summary><code>/comments/1/reaction; /references/0/referenceComments; /references/1/referenceComments</code></details></li><li><a href=\"#reference-12\">PMID:26195800</a><p><strong>Source assertion:</strong> Purified recombinant SQ1 IMG0088 oxidized SLA to SL with both NAD+ and NADP+. Published kinetic constants used succinate semialdehyde because the SLA concentration was undefined; no SLA Km is assigned here.</p><details><summary>Source location</summary><code>//*[@id=&quot;s4&quot;]/p[2]; Table 1 and footnote; Figure 4E-F</code></details></li><li><a href=\"#reference-14\">PMID:37886098</a><p><strong>Source assertion:</strong> The later tetramer and stereoselectivity experiments concern Rhizobium leguminosarum SRDI565 RlGabD, not SQ1. They are not transferred as direct assembly or enantiomer-assay evidence for P0DOV9.</p><details><summary>Source location</summary><code>//*[@id=&quot;abstract1&quot;]/p[1]; //*[@id=&quot;sec3&quot;]/p[1]; //*[@id=&quot;sec6&quot;]/p[1]</code></details></li></ul></td></tr><tr id=\"mechanism-edge-39\"><td>3-sulfolactaldehyde dehydrogenase<br><code>UniProtKB:P0DOV9</code></td><td>enables<p>Alternative NAD